Z||000000||artherd||12-04-2001||12:52 AM||||As I can no longer buy Mobil 1 oil filters here locally, I have switched to K&N's.  I like the 1"/25mm nut which makes them cake to change in and out, and they seem to be a well-made synthetic-element (NOT paper elemnet like everything else!) filter with both good flow and through filtering.<P>The car even seems peppier! (This is straight out of Gran Tourismo 3 video game where you change oil and gain 100hp :)<P>The added touch of safety wire holes in the 25mm nut is just great :)<P>Part number for our cars (88 V6s at least) is HP-2001 and they're less than ten bucks.<P>Just thought I'd share this with the list, if you want your 2.8 to last.<P>Best!<BR>Ben<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
